    {"kind":"takeaways","heading":"The short version","html":"<ul><li>This page is illustrative. It describes a typical deployment in general terms, not a named customer, and invents no quotes, names, numbers, ratings or outcomes.</li><li>Before: a registered manager carried mock inspections and audits in paper folders, written up later from memory.</li><li>After: staff answer checks in WhatsApp as they walk the home, with a photo against each finding.</li><li>The group gains one dashboard across homes, which paper folders could never give.</li><li>The general benefits are less time re-typing notes and evidence captured on the day.</li><li>Quickler is <strong>not</strong> a care records, eMAR or clinical system. Pricing is [[price:bundles]].</li></ul>"},
    {"kind":"default","eyebrow":"Before","heading":"Compliance lived in folders","html":"<p>The starting point is familiar. A registered manager carried the mock CQC or Care Inspectorate walk, the infection control audit and the health and safety walk, on top of running the home. The checks were done on the floor, then written up later at the desk, often from memory at the end of a shift or a week.</p><p>Two problems followed. The record said complete, but the evidence behind it was thin, because it was reconstructed rather than captured as it happened. And the regional lead could not see across the homes, because each home's position lived in a different folder or spreadsheet. See <a href=\"/pages/care-home-compliance-software-uk.html\">care home compliance software</a> for the wider set of checks a home carries.</p>"},
    {"kind":"default","eyebrow":"The change","heading":"The checks moved into WhatsApp","html":"<p>The change is small for staff and large for the record. Each check now arrives as prompts in the staff member's own WhatsApp. There is no app to install and no login. They answer by text when it is quick, and by voice note when their hands are full, as they walk the home rather than afterwards. A photo goes against each finding, timestamped and tied to a location.</p><p>Because the answers are captured on the day, the evidence reflects what was seen, not what was remembered. Each finding becomes an action with an owner and a date, and the finished check produces a shareable web report and a permanent record. See <a href=\"/pages/care-home-audit-software-uk.html\">care home audit software</a> for the mechanics and <a href=\"/pages/quickler-for-care-homes.html\">quickler for care homes</a> for the overview.</p>"},
    {"kind":"default","eyebrow":"After","heading":"What typically improves","html":"<p>In this kind of deployment, the benefits reported are general and consistent. Managers spend less time re-typing notes at the desk, because the record is built as the check is done. The evidence is captured on the day rather than reconstructed, which is exactly what an inspector wants to see. And the group gains a dashboard view across homes that simply did not exist when everything lived in folders.</p><p>We describe these as general patterns, not as measured figures from a named home. We do not have permission to attribute this to a specific customer, so we do not put a name, a quote or a rating on it. If you would like to see whether the same pattern fits your home, the demo runs on your own phone.</p>"},
