  "seoBody": "<h2>An illustrative case study</h2><p>This is a case-study-style account of how a UK care home typically runs its compliance on WhatsApp. To protect confidentiality it is written in general terms, not as a named customer, and it makes no claim about a specific rating, quote or measured outcome. It illustrates the common pattern we see.</p><h2>Before: compliance lived in folders</h2><p>A registered manager carried the mock CQC or Care Inspectorate walk, the infection control audit and the health and safety walk in paper folders, on top of running the home. Checks were done on the floor, then written up later at the desk from memory. The record said complete, but the evidence was thin, and the regional lead could not see across the homes without asking each manager for a spreadsheet.</p><h2>The change: checks moved into WhatsApp</h2><p>Each check now arrives as prompts in the staff member's own WhatsApp. There is no app to install and no login. They answer by text or voice note as they walk the home, with a photo against each finding, timestamped and tied to a location. Because the answers are captured on the day, the evidence reflects what was seen, not what was remembered. Each finding becomes an action with an owner and a date.</p><h2>After: what typically improves</h2><p>In general terms, managers spend less time re-typing notes at the desk, the evidence is captured on the day rather than reconstructed, and the group gains a dashboard view across homes that did not exist when everything lived in folders. We describe these as general patterns, not as measured figures from a named home, and we do not attribute this to a specific customer.</p><h2>What quickler is not</h2><p>Quickler is an audit and evidence tool. It is not a care records system, it is not an eMAR, and it is not a clinical record of any resident. It sits alongside the home's care planning and eMAR system, which stays the single source of truth for anything clinical.</p><h2>Pricing</h2><p>Pricing is only for active users: [[price:bundles]]. An active user completed at least two workflows that month, and dormant users are free.</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>Is this a real named customer?</h3><p>No. To protect confidentiality this page is written in general terms and describes a typical deployment, not a named customer. It invents no quotes, names, numbers, ratings or outcomes.</p><h3>What changes when a care home moves compliance to WhatsApp?</h3><p>Staff answer checks in their existing WhatsApp as they walk the home, rather than writing them up later from memory. A photo goes against each finding on the day, and the group gains one dashboard across homes.</p><h3>Is quickler a care records or eMAR system?</h3><p>No. Quickler is an audit and evidence tool, not a care records, eMAR or clinical system. It sits alongside the home's care records system rather than replacing it.</p>",
